    "text": "Service notice for harbor technicians\n\nStarting May 12, 2033, Mireglass 8.6.2 displays `holdover` when the latest salinity sample is more than 47 seconds old.\n\nIn `holdover`:\n- The panel continues to show the last accepted gate-height estimate.\n- The state does not mean the probe has failed.\n- If the state continues for more than 7 minutes, inspect the intake screen.\n- Do not restart the controller while dive permit `BR-27` is active. Restarting may clear the state from the panel, but it will not unblock the intake.",
